Z||000002||Raydar||06-19-2000||11:16 AM||||A 301?!? <BR>Wasn't that about the lowest performance V-8 that Pontiac ever produced? Or am I thinking of a 307? <BR>With only a few exceptions, I believe that all of the pontiac V-8s were externally identical, from a 326 all the way up to a 455. 301, maybe? Anybody? If that's the case, go for the 455. (Never heard of a Pontiac V8/Fiero swap, though.<BR>I might have said that the guy could have been for real until he said 180 HP from a Duke. <BR>Maybe if you jack up the thermostat and slide a Super Duty underneath it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <BR>Not for $500, though. No way in he!!.<BR>Just my $.02. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfixit58||06-19-2000||11:22 AM||||Why would anybody.... in their right mind... put a 301 in ANYTHING! The motor is a DOG! Externally, it's the almost the same diminsion and ANY other real Pontiac V-8 since 1968. If I were going to all the hassle and expense of a V-8, and I wanted a Pontiac V-8, I wouldn't settle for anyting less than a 400.<P>I would also suspect that, if this guy isn't full of poop, he would have to install the motor longitudnally with a Toranado transmission.<P>Keep us posted,<BR>Roy||||reg||1
Z||000004||phillip||06-20-2000||03:04 AM||||i thought about all the things you all have mentioned during my brief conversation with him. wish i would have had more time to talk with him to either confirm my dought or decide if this was a good opportunity. he said he's seen my car around and from what i can remember of his diertions he lives fairly close or same part of town anyway. i do mean to try and find him.<P>by the way mrfixit, there was a pontiac mag issue around the end of '99 that had a 455 fiero with a riviera tranny. to tell the truth if he could do it that way for that price i'd let him. hate to give up my 5 speed though.<p>[This message has been edited by phillip (edited 06-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||ThatRickGuy||06-20-2000||07:59 PM||||to get a pontiac 455 in a fiero you would have to dow some pretty hefty mods. And yes, everything from the 326 (or was it 327?) to the 455 are identical sized. same blocks, different stroke, bore, and heads. As for the 301... hehe, well, check out <A HREF="http://www.classicalpontiacs.com" TARGET=_blank>www.classicalpontiacs.com</A>  those guys know EVERY THING about pontiac engines. the 301 was a piecer no matter what, bore it, stroke it, throw turbo at it, what ever, a 400 would still take it in the 1/4 mile. I was interested in doing a pontiac engine swap also, but with the differences from pontiac-gm it would be ungodly expencive, but the thought of a torque monster 455 putting out 500 foot pounds of torque in a 2700 pound car!!! OMG! if you could keep the rear end hooked (posi trans axle? super sticky fat tires, and axels the size of my leg) you would be lucky not to get sucked threw the firewall! ||||reg||1
